<!-- core:start -->
When you create a new source file in this project, add the licence header for the file type at the very top of the file, before any code.

Adapt the comment syntax to match the file type as shown below. The templates
below carry the GPL. Where a project licenses part of its tree under a different
licence, the project-specific block at the end of this file defines that variant
and the paths it covers.

The `<year>` and `<copyright holder>` placeholders in these templates are filled
in from the project-specific block at the end of this file. `<year>` is always
the year the file is created.

### JavaScript and Node files (`.mjs`, `.js`, `.cjs`) — `//` comments:

```
// <meta:header>
//   <meta:licence>
//     Copyright (c) <year>, <copyright holder>
//
//     This information is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
//     it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
//     the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
//     (at your option) any later version.
//
//     This information is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
//     but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
//     MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
//     GNU General Public License for more details.
//
//     You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
//     along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
//   </meta:licence>
// </meta:header>
//
// AIMetrics: []
//
```

If the file starts with a shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env node`), the shebang stays on
the first line and the header immediately follows it.

